honeycomb-webrtc patch to WebRTC (webrtc-sdk/webrtc a545de45259b47dfac5f3635863e47cb601f1bb2), D82.
Applied by patches/apply-webrtc-patch.sh in the WebRTC source tree after upstream's
apple_prefix.patch, refused unless every file matches WEBRTC-UPSTREAM.sha256 before and
WEBRTC-PATCHED.sha256 after. Re-derive on every WebRTC commit upgrade.

1. SEC PR-01, frame replay (hive-node wire-protocol.md 6.6 "Replay", D-075, D-086). A frame
   that decrypts plays only if its IV is new for the key it decrypted under: per key and IV
   ssrc, the newest IV timestamp and the IVs within 2 s of the codec clock behind it
   (api/crypto/frame_replay_guard.h). The state lives on the key set: a new key starts empty;
   setting the key a slot already holds keeps it. Nothing resets while the key lives (D-086,
   since build-4): no reset on time, and an ssrc evicted past the 16 live ones is retired for
   the key's life (at most 256; past that, frames of an ssrc not held are refused).
   Tests: api/crypto/frame_replay_guard_unittest.cc (in crypto_unittests), and hive-node's
   frame_replay vectors by tests/frame_replay_guard_test.cc.
2. SEC WEBRTC-01, the RTP audio-level header extensions (ssrc-audio-level, csrc-audio-level),
   which travel outside the frame encryption (wire-protocol.md 6.6): dropped from every parsed
   description at session level and in media sections (api/webrtc_sdp.cc), never offered or
   answered (the voice engine lists ssrc-audio-level as stopped), and never sent whatever was
   negotiated (the audio send channel's extension filter).
3. The key index a played frame decrypted under (honeycomb-ios D156; wire-protocol.md 6.8.1
   "Switching"; since build-4). FrameCryptorTransformerObserver::OnFrameDecryptedWithKeyIndex,
   empty by default, is posted like OnFrameCryptionStateChanged for a receiver's first played
   frame and then only when the index changes (DecryptedKeyIndexReport); only frames that
   decrypted and passed the replay check report. RTCFrameCryptorDelegate gains the @optional
   frameCryptor:didDecryptFrameWithKeyIndex:participantId:.

